# Directories
# NOTE: entries are anchored with a leading "/" (root-relative) on purpose.
# Unanchored patterns match at ANY depth in both `wp dist-archive` and the
# rsync --exclude list built by bin/build-zips.sh — an unanchored "vendor"
# used to strip assets/vendor/ (lucide.min.js) out of the release zip and
# 404 every icon on the frontend. Only .git / node_modules stay unanchored
# (they must never ship at any depth).
.git
node_modules
/.github
/.wordpress-org
/tests
/vendor
/dist
/docs
/bin
/build
# Finder/rsync duplicates ("build 2", "dist 2") are untracked scratch, but the
# anchored /build above does not match them. One such folder put 24 empty
# vendor/squizlabs/... directory entries inside the shipped free zip - no dev
# files, but a wp.org reviewer opening the zip would see a phpcs tree.
/build */
/dist */
/coverage
/audit
/plan
/plans
/.autovap

